course: dictionary
lesson: 1098
title: The brainstem: the automatic life-keeper
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The brainstem is the bottom part of your brain. It joins the brain to the spinal cord, the long cord that runs down your back.
explain: The brainstem runs the jobs your body does without you thinking: breathing, your heartbeat, swallowing and sleeping. You do not have to tell your heart to beat, because the brainstem keeps it going.
explain: Read this sentence: «The left half of the brain controls the right side of the body and the right half controls the left, because nerves cross over in the brainstem, the stalk that joins the brain to the spinal cord.» The words "the stalk that joins" are a clue. A stalk is a thin part that connects two things, so the brainstem is the thin link between the brain and the spinal cord.
fact: The brainstem is the bottom part of the brain.
fact: «Brainstem» means the part of the brain that joins it to the spinal cord.
fact: The brainstem controls automatic actions like breathing, heartbeat, swallowing and sleeping.
fact: Nerves cross over in the brainstem, so the left half of the brain controls the right side of the body.
fact: Helmets protect the head and neck, where the brain, brainstem and spinal cord are.
exercise: What is the brainstem? | The muscle that pumps blood around the body | The part of the brain that does thinking and remembering | *The bottom part of the brain that joins it to the spinal cord | The soft part inside your ear
exercise: Which job does the brainstem control without you thinking? | Solving a maths sum | *Breathing | Choosing your favourite colour | Reading a book
exercise: «The left half of the brain controls the right side of the body...» Find and copy one word that means a thin part that connects. | nerves | controls | *stalk | spinal
test: Why does the left half of the brain control the right side of the body? | *Because nerves cross over in the brainstem | Because the heart is on the left | Because the left side of the body is always stronger | Because the cerebellum controls balance
test: Which of these is NOT an automatic job of the brainstem? | Heartbeat | Sleeping | Swallowing | *Writing a story
exam: Why do helmets protect the head and neck? | To make you look taller | To stop your ears getting cold | *Because the brain, brainstem and spinal cord are there and must be kept safe | To keep your hair dry
